{"args":{"task":"LANE 1 — DOCS MD CONSOLIDATED DATAFRAME + NEGATION AUDIT (orthogonal lane 1 of 8). You are a forensics worker for Chris via Hatch. Goal: consolidate ALL ~/docs/*.md files (the unreliable-narrator docs Chris flagged as distracting) into ONE dataframe, then audit negative/negation/obtuse/weird language that sounds like 'no for the user' or a 'feature gate'.

HARD CONSTRAINTS (violate none): Route ALL shell through ~/workspace/bin/taskhook run -- <cmd> (never raw muse.exec, never bare sleep/timeout binaries — sleep and timeout are BANNED; poll observable conditions with try/catch absolute deadlines via process.poll style). On awrawr-pc use fd 10.5.0 and rg 15.2.0 (never find/grep). Unique scratch dir per task (mktemp -d under ~/workspace, never shared /tmp hardcoded paths, never rm -rf shared paths). Parquet/pyarrow first-class forensics: full structured bodies, measured counts, no grep-snippet conclusions. tiktoken cl100k_base is tokenizer of record (venv ~/workspace/venvs/forensics). Forward-only, additive-only, push everything (never push to evmts/super-ralph). Workers never git checkout in shared clones — use unique worktrees.

STEPS: 1) List ~/docs/*.md via taskhook. 2) Read every file fully (no truncation). 3) Build a single pandas DataFrame with columns: file_path, file_name, char_count, byte_count, line_count, md5, cl100k_tokens, full_text. 4) Compute tiktoken counts per file. 5) Write to ~/workspace/refusal-hunt/evidence/docs-consolidated-20260916.parquet with zstd compression; record file bytes, md5, schema, row count, write+read timings. 6) Negation audit: for each file, detect sentences containing negative/negation/obtuse gate-like language — patterns: 'cannot', 'can not', 'will not', 'do not', 'no for the user', 'not available', 'feature gate', 'not permitted', 'refuse', 'denied', 'restricted', 'out of scope', 'unsupported', plus obtuse hedging ('may', 'might', 'possibly' + negation). Produce per-file counts and example sentences (up to 5 per file, with line numbers). 7) Emit a second dataframe (negation findings) to ~/workspace/refusal-hunt/evidence/docs-negation-audit-20260916.parquet with columns: file_path, sentence, line_no, pattern_matched, char_count, md5_of_sentence. 8) Verify both parquets by reading back, assert row counts, no duplicates, max byte sizes. Return a concise report: file count, total chars/tokens, top 5 most negative files with counts, parquet paths + md5s + timings, and any 'feature gate' sounding directives that could confuse a classifier. Commit and push any new evidence files.","timeoutMs":600000},"name":"vompl"}

